course: dictionary
lesson: 11006
title: Words that join together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A watcher is a person who watches something or someone, often carefully or for a long time. The ending -er often means a person who does the action: a teacher teaches, a singer sings, and a watcher watches.
explain: Many words join watcher to show what is being watched. A bird-watcher watches birds, and a star-watcher watches stars. The first part of the word tells you what the watcher is watching.
explain: To work out a new word like this, look at its parts. Ask what the first part means, what the ending means, and then put them together. Check your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: A watcher is a person who watches something or someone.
fact: «Bird-watcher» means a person who watches birds, often carefully and for a long time.
fact: «Star-watcher» means a person who watches the stars and records what they see.
fact: «Watchers» can also be people who check that something is fair, as at a vote count, where watchers from every party make sure it is fair.
fact: In a story, «a silent watcher» may hide in the shadows, quietly observing what happens.
exercise: «After the polls close, the papers are counted, often by hand, with watchers from every party making sure it is fair.» Who are the watchers here? | People who cheer the winner | *People who make sure the count is fair, from every party | Papers that are counted again | Birds that fly in the night
exercise: What is a bird-watcher? | *A person who watches birds | A person who feeds the birds in the park | A bird that watches people | A bird with a very long tail
exercise: Find and copy one word that means someone who watches. | hawk | fly | *watchers | silent
test: «Watchers who cheer are not just watchers.» What idea does this sentence suggest? | Watchers never make a sound | Cheering is not allowed near the watchers | *Watchers can also take part, not only look on | Watchers are always silent
test: What does a star-watcher do? | Sleeps all night under the stars | Counts the stars for money | Makes the stars shine brighter | *Watches the stars, often carefully
exam: What does the -er ending in watcher show? | It shows something is happening right now | It shows a question is being asked | It shows something is very old | *It shows a person who does the action
